# Every text file keeps LF on every platform. With Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true a checkout
# gets CRLF: a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for 'bash\r' ("no such file or directory"), and a CRLF
# data file (the java-patch fingerprint lists, lib/file-patterns) has a '\r' on every line, so a '^...$'
# match finds nothing (Gen, 19 Nov 2026: the CVE check read the lists as empty). The tree is all text.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
